12
00:57:08,571 --> 00:57:14,571
Extinction is a 2018 American science fiction action film directed by
Ben Young and written by Spenser Cohen and Brad Kane.

13
01:01:54,285 --> 01:02:00,285
The film is about a father who has a recurring dream/vision about the loss of
his family while witnessing an evil force bent on destruction.

14
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
The film stars Michael Peña, Lizzy Caplan, Mike Colter, Lilly
Aspell, Emma Booth, Israel Broussard, and Lex Shrapnel.

15
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
Extinction was filmed over 40 days in Belgrade,
Serbia, on a budget of $20 million.

16
01:16:11,428 --> 01:16:17,428
It had originally been scheduled for a theatrical release on January 26, 2018,
by Universal Pictures, but was pulled from the release schedule.

17
01:20:57,142 --> 01:21:03,142
The film was acquired from Universal by Netflix,
which released it on July 27, 2018.

18
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
It received negative reviews, with criticism for its confused and
weak storyline, character development and pacing.

19
01:30:28,571 --> 01:30:34,571
The film explores themes of monster, amazon rainforest,
jungle, prehistory, prehistoric creature.

20
01:35:14,285 --> 01:35:20,285
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
